    "q-43076": {
      "dom_id": "step-q43076",
      "name": "Question 2",
      "problem": "Suppose $A$ is a $5\\times 5$ matrix and $det(A)=-28.$ The matrix $B$ is obtained from $A$ by applying the elementary row operation ${R}_{5}↔{R}_{3}$ (switching the third and the fifth rows). What is the value of $det(B)?$",
      "worked_solution": "Since swapping any two rows changes the sign of the determinant to the opposite sign, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det(B) & =-det(A) \\\\  & =-(-28) \\\\  & =28.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
