    "q-43077": {
      "dom_id": "step-q43077",
      "name": "Question 6",
      "problem": "Suppose $A$ is a $6\\times 6$ matrix and $det(A)=35.$ The matrix $B$ is obtained from $A$ by applying the elementary row operation ${R}_{1}:=-\\frac{3}{5}{R}_{1}.$ What is the value of $det(B)?$",
      "worked_solution": "The row operation applied to $A$ consists of multiplying a row by the number $-\\frac{3}{5}.$\n\nWhen we do this, the determinant is multiplied by the same number. So, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det(B) & =-\\frac{3}{5}det(A) \\\\  & =-\\frac{3}{5}\\cdot 35 \\\\  & =-21.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
