    "q-72735": {
      "dom_id": "step-q72735",
      "name": "Question 8",
      "problem": "Suppose $B$ is a $6\\times 6$ matrix and $det(B)=80.$ The matrix $C$ is obtained from $B$ by applying the elementary row operation ${R}_{4}:=\\frac{3}{10}{R}_{4}.$ What is the value of $det(C)?$",
      "worked_solution": "The row operation applied to $B$ consists of multiplying a row by the number $\\frac{3}{10}.$\n\nWhen we do this, the determinant is multiplied by the same number. So, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det(C) & =\\frac{3}{10}det(B) \\\\  & =\\frac{3}{10}\\cdot 80 \\\\  & =24.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
