    "q-72731": {
      "dom_id": "step-q72731",
      "name": "Question 9",
      "problem": "Suppose $A$ is a $4\\times 4$ matrix and $det(A)=-64.$ The matrix $B$ is obtained from $A$ by applying the elementary row operation ${R}_{3}:=\\frac{5}{8}{R}_{3}.$ What is the value of $det(B)?$",
      "worked_solution": "The row operation applied to $A$ consists of multiplying a row by the number $\\frac{5}{8}.$\n\nWhen we do this, the determinant is multiplied by the same number. So, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det(B) & =\\frac{5}{8}det(A) \\\\  & =\\frac{5}{8}\\cdot (-64) \\\\  & =-40.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
