      "dom_id": "step-q72462",
      "name": "Question 13",
      "problem": "Suppose $A$ is a $3\\times 3$ matrix and $det(A)=4.$ What is the value of $det(5A)?$",
      "worked_solution": "Multiplying a $n\\times n$ matrix by a scalar $k$ is equivalent to multiplying each row by $k,$ and this occurs $n$ times. This leads to the result\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det(k\\cdot A)={k}^{n}\\cdot det(A).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIn our case, we have $k=5$ and $n=3.$ Therefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det(5A) & ={5}^{3}\\cdot det(A) \\\\  & =125\\cdot 4 \\\\  & =500.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
