    "q-130843": {
      "dom_id": "step-q130843",
      "name": "Question 21",
      "problem": "Given that $det(A)=det(B),$ which of the following elementary row operations transforms matrix $A$ to matrix $B,$ where\n\n$$\nA=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 5 & 3 \\\\ 2 & 4 & -2 \\\\ 2 & 8 & -2\\end{aligned}],\\,B=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 5 & 3 \\\\ 2 & 4 & -2 \\\\ 0 & -2 & -8\\end{aligned}]?\n$$",
      "worked_solution": "Since $det(A)=det(B)$, the row operation applied to $A$ must be to add or subtract a multiple of one row to another row. In other words, it is of the form \n\n$$\n{R}_{j}:={R}_{j}+(k){R}_{i},\\,i\\ne j.\n$$\n\nBy considering the given row operations that are of the above form, we notice that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det(A) & =|\\begin{aligned}1 & 5 & 3 \\\\ 2 & 4 & -2 \\\\ 2 & 8 & -2\\end{aligned}| & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}+(-2){R}_{1} \\\\  & =|\\begin{aligned}1 & 5 & 3 \\\\ 2 & 4 & -2 \\\\ 0 & -2 & -8\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =det(B).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the required row operation is\n\n$$\n{R}_{3}:={R}_{3}+(-2){R}_{1}.\n$$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
